0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the 6502 (NMOS opcodes only), with the data stack
0000                             ;  in zero page
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21). -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace. The break key is checked in the checked build only (at
0000                             ;        every ")" loop-back and every return).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  This is the smaller of the two 6502 interpreters. b8s-6502.asm keeps the
0000                             ;  data stack in pages 2 and 3 (252 cells) and leaves zero page almost free;
0000                             ;  this one keeps it in zero page (112 cells), where the 6502's short
0000                             ;  addressing modes make nearly every handler smaller. The language is the
0000                             ;  same; the memory map and the machine-code contract differ.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One switch, set in the EQU line below:
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks: whatever the spec calls unsafe is not caught
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build, as in the spec's "Errors and checked
0000                             ;                 builds": at startup every word cell points at 0000h (see
0000                             ;                 e_undef) and the variables and the interpreter's cells are
0000                             ;                 0. It stops with S s R r (stack over/underflow), H (heap),
0000                             ;                 O (a store outside the program's space), U (undefined
0000                             ;                 word), Q (no closing quote), W (bad character after [), X
0000                             ;                 (a reserved byte), Z (divide by zero), N (brackets) or B
0000                             ;                 (Ctrl-C), printing the spec's four-line report:
0000                             ;                   Err Z @ 3,4
0000                             ;                   0/ "no"$
0000                             ;                   Stk 2: 5 0
0000                             ;                   Rtn 0
0000                             ;                 and then goes to EXIT.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, C6502 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Registers and zero page
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    IP      zero-page pointer to the next program character (16 bits)
0000                             ;    X       the data-stack pointer. Every cell is two bytes in zero page, low
0000                             ;            byte first: the top cell (TOS) is 0,X and 1,X, the one under it
0000                             ;            (NOS) 2,X and 3,X. The stack grows down: a push is DEX DEX, a
0000                             ;            drop INX INX. A cell that holds an address is used where it is,
0000                             ;            with (0,X): nothing is copied to a pointer first.
0000                             ;    $FE,X   the two bytes under the top cell (zero-page indexing wraps, so
0000                             ;    $FF,X   this is -2,X and -1,X): free memory, used as scratch.
0000                             ;    S       the hardware stack is the RETURN stack: a word call or "(" pushes
0000                             ;            the reading position (high byte first, then low) and "]" or ")"
0000                             ;            pulls it. 100 entries (200 bytes) fit with room to spare.
0000                             ;    Y, A    scratch. Y is 0 after peek/getc.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch: step is called with JSR, so a handler ends with a plain RTS and
0000                             ;  lands on "JMP next" in the loop. Handlers that use the return stack ( ( ) \
0000                             ;  ] 00bbIA== and word calls ) first pull the 2-byte JSR frame off (PLA PLA) and end
0000                             ;  with JMP next instead.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of its
0000                             ;  handler's address, less 1 (the dispatcher pushes an address and "returns"
0000                             ;  to it). The high byte comes from the character: the handlers of the first
0000                             ;  N1 characters start in the image's first page, those of the characters from
0000                             ;  N1 up to N2 in its second, and the rest in its third. The layout below
0000                             ;  keeps to that, and testing/chktab6502.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Every punctuation handler starts with the carry clear (the dispatcher
0000                             ;  leaves it so). Several of them count on that, where the comments say.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Machine-code contract (the grave): the code at TOS is entered as a
0000                             ;  subroutine, by JMP (T0) with the loop's return address on the hardware
0000                             ;  stack, so it ends with RTS (60h, which the hex loader appends). On entry the
0000                             ;  address has been dropped and X is the data-stack pointer: TOS is 0,X (low)
0000                             ;  and 1,X (high), NOS is 2,X and 3,X. To push: DEX, DEX, then store at 0,X
0000                             ;  and 1,X. To drop: INX, INX. The code may change A and Y, and X as the
0000                             ;  stack pointer; it must keep IP ($00/$01) and leave the hardware stack
0000                             ;  balanced. Zero page $02, $03, $07 and $0A-$0D are free for its own use.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                IP:       EQU   00h   ; 00-01 reading position
0000                T0:       EQU   04h   ; scratch
0000                T1:       EQU   05h   
0000                T2:       EQU   06h   
0000                D0:       EQU   08h   ; divisor (division, number printing)
0000                D1:       EQU   09h   
0000                             ; The error report (checked) runs after the program, so it may use the zero
0000                             ; page that machine code has ($02, $03, $0A-$0D; but not $0C-$0D and below
0000                             ; while the report prints, since a full stack reaches down to them):
0000                P:        EQU   02h   ; 02-03 the place being reported
0000                Q:        EQU   0Ah   ; 0A-0B a pointer for counting lines
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    0000-000F  the variables above, and scratch
0000                             ;    0010-00EF  the data stack: 112 cells. X = F0 when it is empty. (0E and
0000                             ;               0F are the scratch under the top cell when it is full.)
0000                             ;    0100-01FF  hardware stack = return stack, S starts at FF
0000                             ;    0400       LET  letter cells: A..Z at +00..+33, a..z at +40..+73 (a word
0000                             ;               cell is 64 bytes below its variable), heap pointer at +7C,
0000                             ;               the -n? line buffer at +80..+FF. The checked build's cells
0000                             ;               are in the gaps: KEYBUF at +34, RSV at +35, PLACE at +36,
0000                             ;               PEND at +38. (+7A and +7B are kept free.)
0000                             ;    0500       PROG the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap follows
0000                             ;    E000       the interpreter (ROM)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the page range LETPAGE..HEAPLIM-1.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (it does
0000                             ;   if the routine ends with LDA / RTS).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve X and Y.
0000                DSE:      EQU   0F0h   ; X when the data stack is empty
0000                DSFULL:   EQU   10h   ; X when it is full
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   04h   
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                PROG:     EQU   0500h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                PROG1:    EQU   PROG+1   
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0E0h   ; the heap must stay below E000h (a page)
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer (the heap top)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+34h   ; a key held back by the break check
0000                RSV:      EQU   LET+35h   ; checked: S as it was before this character
0000                PLACE:    EQU   LET+36h   ; checked: the address of this character
0000                PEND:     EQU   LET+38h   ; checked: the program's end, where the heap
0000                             ;   starts: it may not be released below it
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                LBM1:     EQU   LINEBUF-1   ; (for the error report)
0000                PROGM1:   EQU   PROG-1   
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   20h   ; lowest S allowed (checked build)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                BASE:     EQU   0E000h   ; where the image starts: a multiple of 512
0000                HALFPG:   EQU   BASE/512   ; (the dispatcher doubles this to get a page)
0000                N1:       EQU   8   ; ! " # $ % & ' (  start in the first page,
0000                N2:       EQU   21   ; ) * + , - . / : ; < = > ?  in the second,
0000                             ; @ [ \ ] ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~  in the third
0000                             ; udiv: unsigned TOS / D (D <= 8000h). TOS becomes the quotient; the
0000                             ; remainder is left in the scratch under it, at $FE,X and $FF,X.
0000                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0000                             ; (A macro, because the two builds need it in different places: the
0000                             ; unchecked build uses it to fill the first page.)
0000                .macro UDIV,
0000                             ; 
0000                udiv:   LDA     #0
0000                 STA     0FEh,X
0000                 STA     0FFh,X
0000                 LDA     D0
0000                 EOR     #2
0000                 ORA     D1
0000                 BNE     ud0
0000                 LSR     1,X
0000                 ROR     0,X             ; the quotient
0000                 ROL     0FEh,X          ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0000                 RTS
0000                ud0:    LDY     #16
0000                ud1:    ASL     0,X
0000                 ROL     1,X
0000                 ROL     0FEh,X
0000                 ROL     0FFh,X
0000                 SEC
0000                 LDA     0FEh,X
0000                 SBC     D0
0000                 STA     T0
0000                 LDA     0FFh,X
0000                 SBC     D1
0000                 BCC     ud2
0000                 STA     0FFh,X
0000                 LDA     T0
0000                 STA     0FEh,X
0000                 INC     0,X             ; the quotient bit (bit 0 is free)
0000                ud2:    DEY
0000                 BNE     ud1
0000                 RTS
0000                .endm
0000                 
E000                          .ORG   BASE   
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000                             ;  Page 1 of 3. Startup: find the NUL, the heap starts after it
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000   A2 FF        START:    LDX   #0FFh   
E002   9A                     TXS      ; return stack empty
E003                          IF   CHECKED   
E003                             ; The first half of the letter page is zeroed: every variable, every
E003                             ; cell of the interpreter's own (no key held back), and every word
E003                             ; cell, which then points at 0000h: calling an undefined word stops
E003                             ; with U (see e_undef).
E003   E8                     INX      
E004   8A                     TXA      ; A = 0
E005   A0 7F                  LDY   #7Fh   
E007   99 00 04     STZ:      STA   LET,Y   
E00A   88                     DEY      
E00B   10 FA                  BPL   stz   
E00D                          ENDIF      
E00D   20 EC E4               JSR   rstip   
E010   20 DB E4     ST1:      JSR   getc   
E013   D0 FB                  BNE   st1   ; IP ends just past the NUL
E015   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E017   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E01A                          IF   CHECKED   
E01A   8D 38 04               STA   PEND   
E01D                          ENDIF      
E01D   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E01F   8D 7D 04               STA   HEAP+1   
E022                          IF   CHECKED   
E022   8D 39 04               STA   PEND+1   
E025                          ENDIF      
E025   20 EC E4               JSR   rstip   
E028   A2 F0                  LDX   #DSE   
E02A                             ; ---- the inner loop (the checked build's is further down, out of this page)
E02A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    NEXT:     JSR   step   
                              JMP   next   
E02A                          ENDIF      
E02A                          IF   CHECKED   
E02A   4C 6E E3               JMP   next   
E02D                          ENDIF      
E02D                             ; ---- handlers of ! " # $ % & ' ( : they must start in this page -------------
E02D                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
E02D                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
E02D                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
E02D                             ; The checked build walks a copy of TOS along the string, so that the address
E02D                             ; is still there if it stops with Q on a NUL.
E02D                H_PRINT:      
E02D                          IF   CHECKED   
E02D   20 06 E1               JSR   h_dup   ; the copy
E030   20 3C E0               JSR   pr0   
E033   D0 44                  BNE   pdrop   ; always (X is never 0): drop the address
E035   E8           E_QPR:    INX      
E036   E8                     INX      ; the copy goes: the address is TOS again
E037   A9 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; $ or a string from 22h ran into the end
E039   4C 16 E5               JMP   error   
E03C                PR0:         
E03C                          ENDIF      
E03C   20 80 E2               JSR   tosget   
E03F   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E041   F0 36                  BEQ   pdrop   
E043                          IF   CHECKED   
E043   C9 00                  CMP   #0   
E045   F0 EE                  BEQ   e_qpr   
E047                          ENDIF      
E047   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E049   D0 05                  BNE   pr1   
E04B   20 80 E2               JSR   tosget   
E04E   29 BF                  AND   #0BFh   
E050   20 03 FF     PR1:      JSR   CONOUT   
E053                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JMP   h_print   
E053                          ENDIF      
E053                          IF   CHECKED   
E053   4C 3C E0               JMP   pr0   
E056                          ENDIF      
E056                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
E056   20 56 E4     H_STR:    JSR   puship   
E059                          IF   CHECKED   
E059   20 5F E0               JSR   skipstr   
E05C   F0 D9                  BEQ   e_quote   ; it ran into the end: the place is the 22h
E05E   60                     RTS      
E05F                          ENDIF      
E05F                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
E05F                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it.
E05F                             ; Unchecked, it returns with Z set and A = 22h, and it does not look for the
E05F                             ; end. Checked, it returns with Z clear and A = 11h, or with Z set if the
E05F                             ; text ended first (a NUL, also one just after "/").
E05F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
                              CMP   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMP   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      JSR   incip   
                              BNE   skipstr   ; A is "/" here
E05F                          ENDIF      
E05F                          IF   CHECKED   
E05F   20 DB E4     SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
E062   F0 09                  BEQ   ss9   ; the end
E064   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E066   D0 06                  BNE   ss1   
E068   20 DB E4               JSR   getc   ; the escaped character
E06B   D0 F2                  BNE   skipstr   
E06D   60           SS9:      RTS      ; the end, just after "/"
E06E   C9 22        SS1:      CMP   #22h   
E070   D0 ED                  BNE   skipstr   
E072   4A                     LSR      ; A = 11h, Z clear
E073   60                     RTS      
E074                          ENDIF      
E074   B5 00        H_EMIT:   LDA   0,X   ; "'"
E076   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E079   E8           PDROP:    INX      ; a drop for this page's handlers
E07A   E8                     INX      
E07B   60                     RTS      
E07C                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it. The
E07C                             ; digits are divided off and held on the hardware stack, ended by a 0. udiv
E07C                             ; leaves each remainder in the scratch under the top cell.
E07C   B5 01        H_NUM:    LDA   1,X   
E07E   10 08                  BPL   pn1   
E080   A9 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
E082   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E085   20 F8 E0               JSR   neg   
E088   A9 0A        PN1:      LDA   #10   
E08A   85 08                  STA   D0   
E08C   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E08E   85 09                  STA   D1   
E090   48                     PHA      ; the end marker
E091   20 36 E3     PN2:      JSR   udiv   
E094   B5 FE                  LDA   0FEh,X   
E096   09 30                  ORA   #"0"   
E098   48                     PHA      
E099   B5 00                  LDA   0,X   
E09B   15 01                  ORA   1,X   
E09D   D0 F2                  BNE   pn2   
E09F   68           PN3:      PLA      
E0A0   F0 D7                  BEQ   pdrop   
E0A2   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E0A5   4C 9F E0               JMP   pn3   
E0A8                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ): the low byte, then "."s ending for the high byte.
E0A8   B5 02        H_STORE:   LDA   2,X   
E0AA                          IF   CHECKED   
E0AA   20 29 E3               JSR   chkst   
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD   81 00                  STA   (0,X)   
E0AF   20 82 E2               JSR   inctos   
E0B2   B5 03                  LDA   3,X   
E0B4   4C 0F E1               JMP   st9   
E0B7   B5 00        H_SWAP:   LDA   0,X   ; "%"
E0B9   B4 02                  LDY   2,X   
E0BB   94 00                  STY   0,X   
E0BD   95 02                  STA   2,X   
E0BF   B5 01                  LDA   1,X   
E0C1   B4 03                  LDY   3,X   
E0C3   94 01                  STY   1,X   
E0C5   95 03                  STA   3,X   
E0C7   60                     RTS      
E0C8                             ; "&", and "|" and "^" further down: one byte of the result goes into NOS,
E0C8                             ; and X moves up one. Done twice, that is both bytes, and NOS has become TOS.
E0C8   20 CB E0     H_AND:    JSR   an1   
E0CB   B5 00        AN1:      LDA   0,X   
E0CD   35 02                  AND   2,X   
E0CF   95 02                  STA   2,X   
E0D1   E8                     INX      
E0D2   60                     RTS      
E0D3                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
E0D3                             ; the matching ")".
E0D3   20 66 E4     H_OPEN:   JSR   flag   ; (keeps the carry clear)
E0D6                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skip   
E0D6                          ENDIF      
E0D6                          IF   CHECKED   
E0D6   F0 17                  BEQ   skpar   
E0D8                          ENDIF      
E0D8                             ; pushn: take the step frame off, push the reading position on the return
E0D8                             ; stack, and go on. With the carry set (a word call) the reading position
E0D8                             ; then becomes the address in the letter cell at LET,Y.
E0D8   68           PUSHN:    PLA      
E0D9   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E0DA   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E0DC   48                     PHA      
E0DD   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E0DF   48                     PHA      
E0E0   90 0A                  BCC   nxt   
E0E2   B9 00 04               LDA   LET,Y   
E0E5   85 00                  STA   IP   
E0E7   B9 01 04               LDA   LET+1,Y   
E0EA   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E0EC   4C 6E E3     NXT:      JMP   next   
E0EF                             ; ---- no handler starts between here and the next heading: these routines
E0EF                             ; ---- fill the space up to the page boundary and past it ---------------------
E0EF                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return it in A.
E0EF                             ; Brackets of both kinds count together; strings are stepped over whole. A
E0EF                             ; NUL first ends the program. (The checked build's skip is further down.)
E0EF                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SKIP:     LDA   #0   
                              STA   T2   ; depth
                    SK1:      JSR   getc   
                              BEQ   endprog   
                              CMP   #22h   
                              BNE   sk2   
                              JSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
                    SK2:      CMP   #"("   
                              BEQ   sk3   
                              CMP   #"["   
                              BEQ   sk3   
                              CMP   #")"   
                              BEQ   sk4   
                              CMP   #"]"   
                              BNE   sk1   
                    SK4:      DEC   T2   
                              BPL   sk1   
                              RTS      ; the closer at this level
                    SK3:      INC   T2   
                              BNE   sk1   
                    ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   
E0EF                          ENDIF      
E0EF                          IF   CHECKED   
E0EF                             ; A false ( skips: the wrong closer for it is ].
E0EF   A9 5D        SKPAR:    LDA   #"]"   
E0F1   4C AC E3               JMP   skip   
E0F4                          ENDIF      
E0F4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              ;*Macro unroll:  UDIV
                    UDIV:     LDA   #0   
                              STA   0FEh,X   
                              STA   0FFh,X   
                              LDA   D0   
                              EOR   #2   
                              ORA   D1   
                              BNE   ud0   
                              LSR   1,X   
                              ROR   0,X   
                              ROL   0FEh,X   
                              RTS      
                    UD0:      LDY   #16   
                    UD1:      ASL   0,X   
                              ROL   1,X   
                              ROL   0FEh,X   
                              ROL   0FFh,X   
                              SEC      
                              LDA   0FEh,X   
                              SBC   D0   
                              STA   T0   
                              LDA   0FFh,X   
                              SBC   D1   
                              BCC   ud2   
                              STA   0FFh,X   
                              LDA   T0   
                              STA   0FEh,X   
                              INC   0,X   
                    UD2:      DEY      
                              BNE   ud1   
                              RTS      
E0F4                          ENDIF      
E0F4                             ; absv: TOS = |TOS|.  negm: TOS = -TOS if the N flag is set.
E0F4   B5 01        ABSV:     LDA   1,X   
E0F6   10 0D        NEGM:     BPL   ab9   
E0F8                             ; neg: TOS = -TOS
E0F8   38           NEG:      SEC      
E0F9   A9 00        NEG1:     LDA   #0   
E0FB   F5 00                  SBC   0,X   
E0FD   95 00                  STA   0,X   
E0FF   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E101   F5 01                  SBC   1,X   
E103   95 01                  STA   1,X   
E105   60           AB9:      RTS      
E106                             ; =============================================================================
E106                             ;  Page 2 of 3: handlers of ) * + , - . / : ; < = > ?
E106                             ; =============================================================================
E106   B5 00        H_DUP:    LDA   0,X   ; ":"
E108   B4 01                  LDY   1,X   
E10A   4C 5F E4               JMP   pushay   
E10D                             ; "." ( c addr -- ), and the end of "!": store A at TOS, drop both cells.
E10D   B5 02        H_CSTORE:   LDA   2,X   
E10F                ST9:         
E10F                          IF   CHECKED   
E10F   20 29 E3               JSR   chkst   
E112                          ENDIF      
E112   81 00                  STA   (0,X)   
E114   E8                     INX      
E115   E8                     INX      
E116   E8           DROP:     INX      ; ";"
E117   E8                     INX      
E118   60                     RTS      
E119                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
E119   20 C1 E4     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
E11C   90 0F                  BCC   negnum   
E11E   20 F8 E0     SUB1:     JSR   neg   ; a - b = a + (-b)
E121   18                     CLC      
E122                             ; "+": one byte at a time, as the logic operators do; the carry goes across.
E122                             ; It ends with A = the high byte of the sum.
E122   20 25 E1     H_ADD:    JSR   ad1   
E125   B5 00        AD1:      LDA   0,X   
E127   75 02                  ADC   2,X   
E129   95 02                  STA   2,X   
E12B   E8                     INX      
E12C   60                     RTS      
E12D   A9 00        NEGNUM:   LDA   #0   ; a number from 0 (the digit routine's start)
E12F   20 8D E4               JSR   digit   ; (comes back with the carry set)
E132   B0 C4                  BCS   neg   ; always: the number, negated
E134                             ; Signed compares: a - b sets N and V; N xor V is "a < b". The carry ends up
E134                             ; clear for true, and bool turns it into -1 (true) or 0.
E134   20 B7 E0     H_GT:     JSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
E137   B5 02        H_LT:     LDA   2,X   
