E2BE                             ; ---- machine code: the grave
E2BE                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E2BE                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E2BE                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E2BE                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E2BE                             ; contract in the header.
E2BE   20 CA E4     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E2C1   B0 1C                  BCS   exec   
E2C3   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E2C4   0A                     ASL      
E2C5   0A                     ASL      
E2C6   0A                     ASL      
E2C7   85 04                  STA   T0   
E2C9   20 CA E4               JSR   rdhex   
E2CC   B0 0C                  BCS   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
E2CE   05 04                  ORA   T0   
E2D0   81 00                  STA   (0,X)   ; (never checked)
E2D2   20 82 E2               JSR   inctos   
E2D5   20 CA E4               JSR   rdhex   
