E36E                          IF   CHECKED   
E36E                             ; The checked build's inner loop, out of page 1, where it would not fit.
E36E                NEXT:        
E36E                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, after it has run. The
E36E                             ; return stack has overrun when S is below RSLIM: an overflow leaves
E36E                             ; it at 1Eh or 1Fh, an underflow wraps it to 01h (no handler pulls
E36E                             ; more than one entry). The data stack has when X is above DSE (an
E36E                             ; underflow) or below DSFULL (an overflow). No handler moves X by
E36E                             ; more than 4, so X is caught before it wraps; an overrun by a cell
E36E                             ; or two writes on the scratch bytes below or above the stack.
E36E                             ; S is kept in RSV, for the report's Rtn line (an error found inside
E36E                             ; a handler has its own calls on the hardware stack), and the place
E36E                             ; of the character about to run in PLACE.
E36E   8A                     TXA      ; TSX trashes X: keep it in A
E36F   BA                     TSX      
E370   8E 35 04               STX   RSV   
E373   E0 20                  CPX   #RSLIM   
E375   AA                     TAX      ; TAX leaves the carry alone
E376   90 18                  BCC   e_rstack   
E378   E0 F1                  CPX   #DSE+1   
E37A   B0 26                  BCS   e_sund   
E37C   E0 10                  CPX   #DSFULL   
E37E   90 27                  BCC   e_sovr   
E380   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E382   8D 36 04               STA   PLACE   
E385   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E387   8D 37 04               STA   PLACE+1   
E38A   20 07 E4               JSR   step   
E38D   4C 6E E3               JMP   next   
E390                             ; S/R are overflows, s/r underflows. After an underflow that stack counts as
E390                             ; empty.
E390   AD 35 04     E_RSTACK:   LDA   RSV   
E393   C9 10                  CMP   #10h   
E395   A9 52                  LDA   #"R"   
E397   B0 10                  BCS   ejmp   ; S is 1Eh-1Fh: an overflow
E399   A9 FF                  LDA   #0FFh   
E39B   8D 35 04               STA   RSV   ; S wrapped to 01h: Rtn 0
E39E   A9 72                  LDA   #"r"   
E3A0   D0 07                  BNE   ejmp   ; always
E3A2   A2 F0        E_SUND:   LDX   #DSE   ; Stk 0
E3A4   A9 73                  LDA   #"s"   
E3A6   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E3A7   A9 53        E_SOVR:   LDA   #"S"   
E3A9   4C 16 E5     EJMP:     JMP   error   
E3AC                             ; skip, checked: as the unchecked one above, and A holds, on the way in, the wrong closer for the
E3AC                             ; opener that started the skip, kept in T0: ] for (, ) for [, and 0 for \,
E3AC                             ; which takes either. Meeting the wrong closer at this level, or the end
E3AC                             ; (a NUL, or a string that runs into it), stops with N, except for \,
E3AC                             ; which then ends the program as before.
E3AC   85 04        SKIP:     STA   T0   
E3AE   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E3B0   85 06                  STA   T2   ; depth
E3B2   20 DB E4     SK1:      JSR   getc   
E3B5   F0 26                  BEQ   sknul   
E3B7   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E3B9   D0 05                  BNE   sk2   
E3BB   20 5F E0               JSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 11h, which matches nothing below
E3BE   F0 1D                  BEQ   sknul   ; the string ran into the end
E3C0   C9 28        SK2:      CMP   #"("   
E3C2   F0 15                  BEQ   sk3   
E3C4   C9 5B                  CMP   #"["   
E3C6   F0 11                  BEQ   sk3   
E3C8   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E3CA   F0 04                  BEQ   sk4   
E3CC   C9 5D                  CMP   #"]"   
E3CE   D0 E2                  BNE   sk1   
E3D0   C6 06        SK4:      DEC   T2   
E3D2   10 DE                  BPL   sk1   
E3D4   C5 04                  CMP   T0   
E3D6   F0 0C                  BEQ   e_nest   ; the wrong kind
E3D8   60                     RTS      ; the closer at this level
E3D9   E6 06        SK3:      INC   T2   
E3DB   D0 D5                  BNE   sk1   
E3DD   A5 04        SKNUL:    LDA   T0   
E3DF   D0 03                  BNE   e_nest   ; ( and [ stop with N
E3E1   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   ; \ ends the program
E3E4   A9 4E        E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [ found the wrong closer
E3E6   4C 16 E5               JMP   error   ;   or the end: the place is the opener
E3E9                          ENDIF      
E3E9                          IF   CHECKED   
E3E9   A9 58        E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte, 80h-FFh
E3EB   4C 16 E5     EJMP2:    JMP   error   
E3EE                             ; e_undef: the word cells of undefined words hold 0000h. A call there reads
E3EE                             ; the byte at 0000h, which is IP's own low byte: 00h while IP is 0000h, so
E3EE                             ; the call reads a NUL with IP in page zero, where no program can be. The
E3EE                             ; call is undone first: the step frame and the return address come off the
E3EE                             ; hardware stack, and the place is the call letter (the return address - 1).
E3EE   68           E_UNDEF:   PLA      
E3EF   68                     PLA      ; the step frame
E3F0   68                     PLA      
E3F1   38                     SEC      
E3F2   E9 01                  SBC   #1   
E3F4   8D 36 04               STA   PLACE   
E3F7   68                     PLA      
E3F8   E9 00                  SBC   #0   
E3FA   8D 37 04               STA   PLACE+1   
E3FD   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   
E400   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   ; Rtn does not count the call
E403   A9 55                  LDA   #"U"   
E405   D0 E4                  BNE   ejmp2   ; always
E407                          ENDIF      
E407                             ; step: read one character and sort it by range.
E407                             ;    00h          end of program
E407                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored
E407                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
E407                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
E407                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
E407                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
E407   20 DB E4     STEP:     JSR   getc   ; flags follow A
E40A   F0 3D                  BEQ   endp   
E40C   38                     SEC      
E40D   E9 21                  SBC   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
E40F   90 37                  BCC   ign   ; 01h-20h
E411   C9 0F                  CMP   #0Fh   
E413   90 24                  BCC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: index 0-14
E415   E9 0F                  SBC   #0Fh   ; (carry set) A = c - 30h
E417   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E419   90 72                  BCC   digit   
E41B   C9 11                  CMP   #11h   
E41D   90 18                  BCC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
E41F   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (carry set) A = c - 41h
E421   C9 1A                  CMP   #1Ah   
E423   90 2B                  BCC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah
E425   C9 20                  CMP   #20h   
E427   90 0C                  BCC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
E429   C9 3A                  CMP   #3Ah   
E42B   90 2F                  BCC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h
E42D   C9 3E                  CMP   #3Eh   
E42F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BCS   ign   ; 7Fh-FFh
E42F                          ENDIF      
E42F                          IF   CHECKED   
E42F   F0 17                  BEQ   ign   ; 7Fh
E431   B0 B6                  BCS   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
E433                          ENDIF      
E433                             ; The three adjustments below chain. Each ADC adds the carry the one
E433                             ; before it left, which the constants allow for.
E433   E9 1A                  SBC   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: (carry clear: -1Bh) index 28-31
E435   69 F6        P5B:      ADC   #0F6h   ; 5Bh-60h: -10 (-9 when chained), index 22-27
E437   69 05        P3A:      ADC   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: +5 (+6 when chained), index 15-21
E439                             ; Punctuation: A = the index. The handler's page is the first, plus one if
E439                             ; the index is N1 or more, plus one more if it is N2 or more.
E439   C9 08        PUNCT:    CMP   #N1   
E43B   A8                     TAY      
E43C   A9 70                  LDA   #HALFPG   
E43E   2A                     ROL      ; the first page, or the second (carry clear)
E43F   C0 15                  CPY   #N2   
E441   69 00                  ADC   #0   ; ... or the third (and the carry is clear)
E443   48                     PHA      
E444   B9 6D E4               LDA   PTAB,Y   
E447   48                     PHA      
E448   60           IGN:      RTS      ; RTS trick: goes to the handler. Reached
E449                             ; directly, it just ends an ignored character.
E449                ENDP:        ; the program has ended
E449                          IF   CHECKED   
E449   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   ; IP in page zero: an undefined word
E44B   F0 A1                  BEQ   e_undef   
E44D                          ENDIF      
E44D   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E450                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
E450                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
E450   0A           UPPER:    ASL      
E451   A8                     TAY      
E452   38                     SEC      
E453   4C D8 E0               JMP   pushn   
E456   A5 00        PUSHIP:   LDA   IP   ; push the reading position
E458   A4 01                  LDY   IP+1   
E45A   D0 03                  BNE   pushay   ; always: no program is in page zero
E45C                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
E45C   0A           LOWER:    ASL      
E45D   A0 04                  LDY   #>LET   
E45F                             ; pushay: push a cell: A = its low byte, Y = its high byte
E45F   CA           PUSHAY:   DEX      
E460   CA                     DEX      
E461   95 00        SETAY:    STA   0,X   ; setay: TOS = A (low), Y (high)
E463   94 01                  STY   1,X   
E465   60                     RTS      
E466                             ; flag: pops TOS and returns with Z set if it was 0. Keeps the carry.
E466   E8           FLAG:     INX      
E467   E8                     INX      
E468   B5 FE                  LDA   0FEh,X   
E46A   15 FF                  ORA   0FFh,X   
E46C   60                     RTS      
E46D                             ; =============================================================================
E46D                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of (handler - 1) for each punctuation
E46D                             ;  character, in code order.
E46D                             ; =============================================================================
E46D   A7           PTAB:     DB   (h_store-1) & 0FFh   ; !
E46E   55                     DB   (h_str-1) & 0FFh   ; "
E46F   7B                     DB   (h_num-1) & 0FFh   ; #
E470   2C                     DB   (h_print-1) & 0FFh   ; $
E471   B6                     DB   (h_swap-1) & 0FFh   ; %
E472   C7                     DB   (h_and-1) & 0FFh   ; &
E473   73                     DB   (h_emit-1) & 0FFh   ; '
E474   D2                     DB   (h_open-1) & 0FFh   ; (
E475   B4                     DB   (h_close-1) & 0FFh   ; )
E476   57                     DB   (h_mul-1) & 0FFh   ; *
E477   21                     DB   (h_add-1) & 0FFh   ; +
E478   AB                     DB   (h_cfetch-1) & 0FFh   ; ,
E479   18                     DB   (h_sub-1) & 0FFh   ; -
E47A   0C                     DB   (h_cstore-1) & 0FFh   ; .
E47B   82                     DB   (h_div-1) & 0FFh   ; /
E47C   05                     DB   (h_dup-1) & 0FFh   ; :
E47D   15                     DB   (drop-1) & 0FFh   ; ;
E47E   36                     DB   (h_lt-1) & 0FFh   ; <
E47F   47                     DB   (h_eq-1) & 0FFh   ; =
E480   33                     DB   (h_gt-1) & 0FFh   ; >
E481   BB                     DB   (h_key-1) & 0FFh   ; ?
E482   72                     DB   (h_fetch-1) & 0FFh   ; @
E483   99                     DB   (h_def-1) & 0FFh   ; [
E484   18                     DB   (h_break-1) & 0FFh   ; \
E485   2C                     DB   (h_ret-1) & 0FFh   ; ]
E486   5C                     DB   (h_xor-1) & 0FFh   ; ^
E487   EB                     DB   (h_alloc-1) & 0FFh   ; _
E488   BD                     DB   (h_grave-1) & 0FFh   ; `
E489   40                     DB   (h_tor-1) & 0FFh   ; {
E48A   67                     DB   (h_or-1) & 0FFh   ; |
E48B   4C                     DB   (h_fromr-1) & 0FFh   ; }
E48C   59                     DB   (h_not-1) & 0FFh   ; ~
E48D                             ; Digits: the first one is in A; read the rest of the number.
E48D   A0 00        DIGIT:    LDY   #0   
E48F   20 5F E4               JSR   pushay   
E492                             ; rdnum: TOS = TOS*10 + digit for each digit at IP. Wraps at 16 bits.
E492                             ; Returns with the carry set.
E492   20 C1 E4     RDNUM:    JSR   isdig   
E495   B0 4F                  BCS   ic9   ; (an RTS)
E497   20 DE E4               JSR   incip   ; (keeps A = the digit)
E49A   16 00                  ASL   0,X   
E49C   36 01                  ROL   1,X   ; x2
E49E   18                     CLC      
E49F   75 00                  ADC   0,X   
E4A1   85 04                  STA   T0   
E4A3   B5 01                  LDA   1,X   
E4A5   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E4A7   85 05                  STA   T1   ; T = x2 + digit
E4A9   16 00                  ASL   0,X   
E4AB   36 01                  ROL   1,X   
E4AD   16 00                  ASL   0,X   
E4AF   36 01                  ROL   1,X   ; x8
E4B1   18                     CLC      
E4B2   B5 00                  LDA   0,X   
E4B4   65 04                  ADC   T0   
E4B6   95 00                  STA   0,X   
E4B8   B5 01                  LDA   1,X   
E4BA   65 05                  ADC   T1   
E4BC   95 01                  STA   1,X   ; x8 + x2 + digit
E4BE   4C 92 E4               JMP   rdnum   
E4C1                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is clear if it is a
E4C1                             ; digit. Y = 0.
E4C1   20 E7 E4     ISDIG:    JSR   peek   
E4C4   38                     SEC      
E4C5   E9 30                  SBC   #"0"   
E4C7   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E4C9   60                     RTS      
E4CA                             ; rdhex: if IP is at a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), return its value in A with
E4CA                             ; the carry clear and IP moved on; otherwise the carry is set and IP stays.
E4CA   20 C1 E4     RDHEX:    JSR   isdig   
E4CD   90 0F                  BCC   incip   
E4CF   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   
E4D1   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (the carry is set)
E4D3   C9 06                  CMP   #6   
E4D5   B0 0F                  BCS   ic9   
E4D7   69 0A                  ADC   #10   
E4D9   D0 03                  BNE   incip   ; always
E4DB                             ; Reading the program
E4DB                             ;    peek: A = the character at IP, IP unchanged, Y = 0
E4DB                             ;    getc: the same, then IP moves on; flags follow A
E4DB                             ;    incip: IP moves on; keeps A, the carry and Y
E4DB   20 E7 E4     GETC:     JSR   peek   
E4DE   E6 00        INCIP:    INC   IP   
E4E0   D0 02                  BNE   ic1   
E4E2   E6 01                  INC   IP+1   
E4E4   09 00        IC1:      ORA   #0   
E4E6   60           IC9:      RTS      
E4E7   A0 00        PEEK:     LDY   #0   
E4E9   B1 00                  LDA   (IP),Y   
E4EB   60                     RTS      
E4EC                             ; rstip: point IP at the start of the program
E4EC   A9 00        RSTIP:    LDA   #<PROG   
E4EE   85 00                  STA   IP   
E4F0   A9 05                  LDA   #>PROG   
E4F2   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E4F4   60                     RTS      
E4F5                             ; =============================================================================
E4F5                             ;  Console layer: getk returns a waiting key in A (zero flag clear), or
E4F5                             ;  A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. CONOUT prints A.
E4F5                             ;  Both keep X and Y. In the unchecked build getk is the host's KEY itself.
E4F5                             ; =============================================================================
E4F5                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    GETK:     EQU   KEY   ; the host's routine does the whole job
E4F5                          ENDIF      
E4F5                          IF   CHECKED   
E4F5   AD 34 04     GETK:     LDA   KEYBUF   ; a key held back by the break check
E4F8   F0 08                  BEQ   gk1   
E4FA   48                     PHA      
E4FB   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E4FD   8D 34 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E500   68                     PLA      
E501   60                     RTS      
E502   4C 06 FF     GK1:      JMP   KEY   
E505                             ; =============================================================================
E505                             ;  Checked build: break key and error reports
E505                             ; =============================================================================
E505                             ; chkbrk: a waiting key is read now; Ctrl-C stops the program, anything
E505                             ; else is held for the next "?". Keeps the flags.
E505   08           CHKBRK:   PHP      
E506   20 F5 E4               JSR   getk   
E509   F0 07                  BEQ   cb9   
E50B   C9 03                  CMP   #3   
E50D   F0 05                  BEQ   e_break   
E50F   8D 34 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E512   28           CB9:      PLP      
E513   60                     RTS      
E514   A9 42        E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C
E516                             ; error: the report, then EXIT. A = the letter, PLACE = the place, X = the
E516                             ; data stack to show, RSV = S for the Rtn line. Nothing here relies on S: an
E516                             ; overflowed or underflowed hardware stack wraps inside its page, and only
E516                             ; its depth is shown.
E516                             ;   CR LF
E516                             ;   Err X @ line,col CR LF
E516                             ;   up to 16 characters from the place, raw, up to a CR, LF or NUL  CR LF
E516                             ;   Stk n: [...] and the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top  CR LF
E516                             ;   Rtn n CR LF
E516                             ; The numbers go through "#" (prnum), which pushes them over the data stack
E516                             ; and pops them again, so the stack is shown as it was. With the stack full
E516                             ; (X = 0Eh) that reaches down to 0Ah, so nothing the report keeps is there.
E516   48           ERROR:    PHA      ; the letter
E517   AD 36 04               LDA   PLACE   
E51A   85 02                  STA   P   
E51C   AD 37 04               LDA   PLACE+1   
E51F   85 03                  STA   P+1   
